## 5. The vLLM situation (OPEN DECISION — was pending when session ended)

vLLM **0.22.0 ships only `cu129` and `cu13` GPU wheels — no `cu128`.** Checked
0.19–0.22: all cu129 or cu13/cu130. So on the *current* 570.169 driver, no vllm
GPU wheel runs (cu129 needs ≥575, cu13 needs ≥580), and cu129 would also conflict
with torch cu128's nvidia-12.8 libs. vLLM therefore currently sits in the lock as
cu13 and imports with an Unsloth warning but **does not run on a 12.8 driver**.
This does NOT affect training (SFT doesn't use vLLM).

Why `vllm>=0.19`? Not a feature requirement — bumped from `>=0.13` in commit
`96cb185` ("Experiment with Gemma 4") alongside `transformers==5.2.0`. It's the
vllm floor that lines up with transformers 5.x. So we can't drop below it without
risking transformers-5 support (which we need).

