## 6. Driver upgrade cheatsheet (run on the HOST, not the container)

```bash
# record state for rollback
nvidia-smi; uname -r; lsb_release -a; mokutil --sb-state
sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y linux-headers-$(uname -r) build-essential
# NVIDIA CUDA repo (adjust ubuntu2404 to host version)
wget https://developer.download.nvidia.com/compute/cuda/repos/ubuntu2404/x86_64/cuda-keyring_1.1-1_all.deb
sudo dpkg -i cuda-keyring_1.1-1_all.deb && sudo apt-get update
# stop GPU workloads / containers first, then install ONLY the driver (open modules)
sudo apt-get install -y cuda-drivers-580      # 580 branch = CUDA 13
sudo reboot
# after reboot:
nvidia-smi                                    # expect 580.xx, "CUDA Version: 13.x", both 3090s
sudo systemctl restart docker                 # then rebuild/reopen the devcontainer
```
Gotchas: Secure Boot must be off or MOK-enrolled or the module won't load; don't
mix `.run` + apt installs (purge `^nvidia-.*` `^cuda-.*` first if a `.run` driver
was used); 3090 (Ampere) supports the open kernel modules on 580.

